{title:The Catcher}
{key:}

If I was pure chaos and you were dead calm
We could conjure a new type of storm
In the fusion of opposites magic can happen 
And sometimes a miracle is born
A color that cannot tell black from white
A scarecrow that laughs all day long
A rain shower that is afraid of a rainbow
A silence that is in love with a song
So never mind that we are both just flesh and bone
You and I are free to entertain any possible thought
I'll bring the chaos if you bring the calm
Together we just might catch 
Some thing that cannnot be caught
